@page
@model Portfolio.Pages.PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

    <div class="about-bio">
        <p>
            This page explains what happens to your information when you use this website,
            in plain language.
        </p>

        <h2>What I collect</h2>
        <p>
            This site does not use cookies, tracking scripts, or analytics. The only
            information collected is what you choose to submit through the
            <a asp-page="/Contact" class="footer-link">Contact form</a>: your name, email
            address, and message.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's used</h2>
        <p>
            When you submit the contact form, your message is sent directly to my email
            inbox so I can read and reply to it. Your information is never sold, shared
            with third parties, or used for anything other than responding to you.
        </p>

        <h2>How long it's kept</h2>
        <p>
            Submitted messages live in my personal email inbox for as long as I keep that
            conversation, the same as any other email you'd send me directly. This site
            itself does not store your data in a database.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            If you'd like me to delete a message you've sent, or have any questions about
            your data, just email me at
            <a href="mailto:vic.jaq91@protonmail.com" class="footer-link">vic.jaq91@protonmail.com</a>
            and I'll take care of it.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>